  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Writing for this book began at Paper &amp; Book Intensive (PBI) at Oxbow School of Art in Saugatuck, Michigan, May 2017. Editing was completed in New Haven, Connecticut. The design and collages were undertaken in Claremont, California."-- Colophon</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="505" ind1="0" ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">One. Conception -- *The asterisk. or Maybe -- Two. Editing -- Three. Image making -- Four. Printing -- Five. Binding -- Six. Editioning -- Seven. Exhibiting -- Eight. Selling -- Nine. Presenting -- Ten. Acquisitions -- Eleven. (Bonus track) -- Colophon</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Text of concrete poems and prose set against an illustrated background of collage work</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"For just over a year, I had been working on a project about love, or trying to at least. Then I accepted that I was not in love with any person. There was no man with whom I wanted to connect, but there was love of craft, of practice, of field. With that realization, this project quickly came together. I hope this book speaks more eloquently that I on my process of creating an artist's book from conception to the last stitch and beyond."-- Colophon</subfield>
  </datafield>
